        "id": 9142
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-11-02T08:43:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why does Identity need to know that Resource backend even exists?\nI guess it\u0027s because we have user inside a domain.\n\nBut what about removing this dependency here?\nWe could have a special assignment to an entity from Identity on a resource from Resource with a role \u0027owned_by\u0027.\n\nThis way, potential advantages are:\n1) We have no dependency between Identity and Resource; \n2) We could even have user/group owned by projects (reseller ?);\n3) We could have a user/group with multiple parents (actor inside different projects, domains).",
      "revId": "3f6031375c1e384b5052c1f8b5deeb32f7f490ad",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
